         <notesStmt>
            <note type="project" target="#dat1">Whitman's notes on this manuscript provide useful but puzzling information regarding the timeframe in which it was written. The note at the upper right suggests that Whitman sent  a finished version of the poem to the <hi rend="italic">New York Herald</hi> on 21 April 1887, over nine months before it was published there.</note>
            <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00314" cert="high">"To Those Who've Fail'd" first appeared in print in the 27 January 1888 issue of the <hi rend="italic">New York Herald</hi>. Whitman included a revised version in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi> (1888) and in the "Sands at Seventy" annex to later printings of <hi rend="italic">Leaves of Grass</hi>.</note>
         </notesStmt>
